# PoC architecture: Fargate uses public subnet + IGW instead of VPC Interface Endpoints.
# Egress is restricted to port 443 only — Trivy checks IP range, not port range.
# Risk accepted: all outbound traffic is HTTPS to AWS services only.
AWS-0104

# CVE reports + SBOM buckets use SSE-S3 (AWS-owned key), not a customer managed
# key. CMK removed 2026-07-16 per Phase3DeploymentPlanPoC.md item 9 as part of
# the cost-reduction pass (dedicated Phase 2 KMS CMK decommissioned). Risk
# accepted: this is a portfolio project, data is Trivy/Syft scan output (CVE
# reports, SBOMs) rather than sensitive customer data, and SSE-S3 still
# provides encryption at rest -- just without customer-managed key rotation
# and access-policy control.
AWS-0132
